// tests/fixtures/err_no_such_builtin_method_dict.ubl
// Regression test for a `SemaType::display()` bug (docs/DIAGNOSTICS_RULES.md
// §8, second case study): `display()` explicitly handled a dozen-or-so
// SemaType variants and fell through a `_ => "<type>".into()` catch-all for
// everything else, including `Dictionary`. Every prior NoSuchMethod fixture
// happened to use a `List` receiver, so this gap was never exercised — the
// error message would have read `type <type> has no method frobnicate`
// instead of naming the real type.
//
// Expected: sema FAIL (NoSuchMethod), with the `on_type` field rendering as
// `Dictionary<?T1, ?T2>`, not `<type>`.

fn main() void {
    let ages = Dictionary.new()
    ages.insert("alice", 31)
    ages.frobnicate()
}
